{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit","id":63827,"title":"Removing Luncay and Gauru Time Limit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-03T01:43:11-08:00","id":63827,"title":"Removing Luncay and Gauru Time Limit","content":"A few people on the thread for the Idigam Chronicle ideas have suggested removing Lunacy and/or the time limit for Gauru form.<br /> <br /> I know they'll be many in favour and some vehemently <i>against</i>.<br /> <br /> How do people think that altering the game by removing one or both of these would change the it - what are the pros and cons of doing so?<br /> <br /> If you wouldn't remove either/both would you consider increasing the time limit or weakening the powers of lunacy? If so why?<br /> <br /> I'm going to go suggest for the scope of this thread that nothing else is being under consideration for change.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> My personal choice would be to 1. see if anyone responds to the thread and see what others think first 2. be inclined to think that I would like to see them both as optional, with perhaps a sidebar in the Idigam Chronicle as to why. 3. I tended to downplay both of them in my game I ran but did include them.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: this is just a personal preference, but if Garou form remains time limited I would very much like to see artwork that mirrors this, as the core book doesn't really reflect this (although the artwork is very good)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":510,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","user":"MeetsInTaverns","date":". 02-03-2014, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T02:03:28-08:00","id":63833,"title":"","content":"Con against removing the Gauru time limit - the balance between the form statistics is destroyed. The war form loses much of its thematic focus and everything that makes it special.<br /> <br /> Pro for removing Lunacy - the Masquerade turns into a new thematic big thing for Werewolf, an additional complication. One might also see this as a con - the Forsaken have it difficult enough as it is - I can see the merit in both approaches.<br /> <br /> Con against removing Lunacy - the wolfblooded merit loses much of its thematic focus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T02:19:03-08:00","id":63842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=63833#post63833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Con against removing the Gauru time limit - the balance between the form statistics is destroyed. The war form loses much of its thematic focus and everything that makes it special.<br /> <br /> Pro for removing Lunacy - the Masquerade turns into a new thematic big thing for Werewolf, an additional complication. One might also see this as a con - the Forsaken have it difficult enough as it is - I can see the merit in both approaches.<br /> <br /> Con against removing Lunacy - the wolfblooded merit loses much of its thematic focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some have said* that with the time limit as it stands that Gauru is too near to Urshul to be worth changing to. Would you think that if the time limit stands as is that Gauru's war form should have a bit of a buff to really drive home the thematic focus?<br /> <br /> *citation needed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T02:29:38-08:00","id":63843,"title":"","content":"Yes, I do - I think that Gauru as per the official rules needs to be more powerful.<br /> <br /> I like the time limit. If I get my way, it remains.<br /> <br /> In my homebrew rules, there's no time limit on Gauru, technically, but using it gets you closer to Death Rage. There should always be a risk involved when taking on the war form. It's powerful, but you aren't really in control.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T02:58:28-08:00","id":63852,"title":"","content":"Would you feel that you could remove the time limit on Gauru if it got you closer to Death Rage officially in the core?<br /> <br /> I have heard before that folk wouldn't want the time limit taken out of the book because of thematic reasons, yet still either houserule it out or change it significantly as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T03:05:50-08:00","id":63853,"title":"","content":"It would need to be a consecutive thing, where you get closer and closer to Death Rage the longer you remain in Gauru. In my game, the players have to consider the tactical advantages of staying in Gauru vs. taking on a safer but less powerful form every turn. We kind of liked that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:00:35-08:00","id":63986,"title":"","content":"For myself, if I were to remove one or the other, it would be to remove Lunacy and rely on the fact that if people see a giant wolf-man looking thing coming at them, they're gonna panic and run. I don't like that there is a forced mechanism preventing the guys who want to charge forward and attack from doing just that. I realize it takes balls of brass to not run in the face of that, but there are some guys brave or stupid enough to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:23:58-08:00","id":64002,"title":"","content":"I for one, don't mind Lunacy. It can stay but I want it to be something like the Predator's Aura from B&amp;S. Something you can turn on or off. However, the Gauru time limit needs to be thrown into a fire somewhere. Seriously, it doesn't need to be there. The form already has too many limitations as is. Either the time limit needs to go, or a few other restrictions need to be removed and Gauru made stronger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":427,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","user":"Rahuman101","date":". 02-03-2014, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/427-rahuman101","name":"Rahuman101","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar427_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:29:21-08:00","id":64010,"title":"","content":"I must say I do like the idea of Lunacy being something you have to actively invoke.<br /> <br /> I'm starting to wish there wasn't a time limit at all, but that could be a throwback to apocalypse. I think removing the limit, increasing the strength but making you more of a raging monster &quot;might&quot; do it. Perhaps I'd just prefer a whole bunch of &quot;tailor your garou form this way or that&quot; options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T08:38:20-08:00","id":64022,"title":"","content":"I am in disagreement with the time-limit being removed. That said I am for a buff in war forms capabilities... but only slightly, not a gigantic leap. That would make players take the garou every 5 seconds. There is already a story line from the chronicles book that creates a fetish that eliminates the time limit, so there's already a work up for that. <br /> <br /> As for Lunacy, they could remove it, so long as there are adequate change ups for it. I think there was already a work up for that too though... course I may be wrong. I know there was a work up in the chronicles book for Uratha to be able to mate with each other. Brought up some interesting harmony violations. &quot;Duty by mate&quot; and &quot;duty by pack&quot; may conflict, leading to some very interesting drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T09:05:27-08:00","id":64040,"title":"","content":"While I do think that the rules for each concept need work, I'd rather not see either go.<br /> <br /> Lunacy is a benefit for the Uratha. One of the few tools they all have. And even then it isn't a perfect shield. Any decent werewolf-hunter (or simply other werewolf) is going to be able to spot Lunacy incidents when they happen. Unless the rules are changed significantly, why would an Uratha every choose not to invoke Lunacy? The only significant circumstance I can think of would be defending someone subject to it that is also a significant factor in the fight (like a highly trained wolf-blooded combatant). But then your enemies (if they are werewolves which make up a lot of your physical enemies) would want to invoke it at them.<br /> <br /> I think the easier solution is to let characters choose to take a &quot;Terrified&quot; Condition automatically/use the chart (aka what most NPCs will do) or roll Resolve + Composure (+modifiers for non-Gauru form) and have a wider array of Condition possibilities. Dramatic failure goes back to being Terrified, failure lets the Uratha's player pick from 3 Conditions, success lets the human pick from the same list, and exceptional success lets them off Condition free. Basically have it work similar to a breaking point check with a bit more direction on the difference between regular failures and successes.<br /> <br /> I've always been a fan of the time limit hack that treats your base-time limit as your &quot;safe&quot; turns before you start rolling for Kuruth rather than an absolute limit. Given the relatively short durations of most fights in the nWOD (esp. with the GMC rules) the time limit has never been as onerous as I see people make it out to be. The GMC rules also already boost the Gauru forms power via the increased Defense. The extra attack dice generated by the bonus Strength means that blowing through the increased Defense is that much easier to do reliably. Sure it is still only one more than the next best form, but attack dice are essentially worth more now; and armor is worth more now as well.<br /> <br /> Giving the Gauru form a bit more oomph (like boosting the damage ratings on its claws/bites or X-again bonuses) wouldn't be a bad thing along with the gamble to stay fighting option. But the time limit doesn't really need to go for any particular reason. And we certainly don't need to return to &quot;sitting around in war form&quot; as a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T09:11:04-08:00","id":64047,"title":"","content":"When would a werewolf not choose to invoke it? Well perhaps it's something that has to be used on someone - if the werewolf is not aware of that person then they wouldn't be able to use it. And I wouldn't think that there are a lot of times a human is going to sneak up on a werewolf.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of your condition mind.<br /> <br /> As for the time limit - I like the idea of it in game, but honestly when I found that combats didn't last that long and it wasn't much of an issue. From what I remember (and it's a while since I ran my forsaken game) the limit is usually only in seconds. It just seems strange to me that a werewolf transforms into it's fighting form for basically a few seconds - especially as it's not that much beefier (and lower on dex) than other forms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T11:24:37-08:00","id":64149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MeetsInTaverns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=64047#post64047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When would a werewolf not choose to invoke it? Well perhaps it's something that has to be used on someone - if the werewolf is not aware of that person then they wouldn't be able to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very big change from the original Lunacy though. As is, Lunacy applies to all human on-lookers. Having to actively invoke Lunacy on individuals is a massive decrease in its utility. Now, letting werewolves let a bit of that rage simmering beneath the surface out to intimidate others (instead of just not sucking at Intimidation and being penalized at other social Skills), would be a nice adjustment to the rules; but that seems like it should go under Primal Urge changes not Lunacy changes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the idea of your condition mind. </div> </div> </div>Thanks, though I can't say it's original in the slightest. There's been plenty of talk about using Conditions with Lunacy already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From what I remember (and it's a while since I ran my forsaken game) the limit is usually only in seconds. It just seems strange to me that a werewolf transforms into it's fighting form for basically a few seconds - especially as it's not that much beefier (and lower on dex) than other forms. </div> </div> </div>The actual maximum duration is between 6 and 75 seconds IIRC; which isn't a lot in real time but is tons in combat. But that's under control. In Death Rage a werewolf could be in Gauru for hours.<br /> <br /> Again though, the GMC rules make the Gauru form, with no changes, a lot more dangerous than the other options. It is, to an extent, &quot;beefier&quot; without any changes.<br /> <br /> The toning back of Fighting Styles and improved Grappling rules make Dalu less competitive than Gauru if you're using weapons, since Gauru gets the Health, armor, and Strength boosts.<br /> <br /> The increased damage done with the new weapon rules also make the Gauru form's ability to use weapons a huge boost over Urshul. In the pre-GMC rules it amounted to a 1-4 dice difference at best (1 for the increased strength, and the 1-3 extra being for using weapons with a damage rating of 3-5). In the GMC rules having a 4L Fetish weapon and armor vs the 2L bites of Urshul is a pretty significant game changer (assuming bites don't get decreased to 1L on top of it).<br /> <br /> Though one thing to consider is not that the time-limit gets changed (since the time-limit is not nearly as taxing as it seems), but the number of activations of Gauru per scene becoming variable.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of people would be happier if, for example, instead of one Gauru form use a scene, you could rest for 11-Primal Urge minutes to regain your self-control (or making it an extended meditation roll or something) and then go again. That way timing your use of Gauru form in a fight remains a tactical decision, but in a scene that might have multiple fights with some gaps between them, you don't have to save up your Gauru use for what you hope is the right time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:00:08-08:00","id":64242,"title":"","content":"Here's the thematic implications of having a Lunacy with a switch on/off button; or removing it entirely: It's implied the mild form of social discomfort that humans suffer and hinder Uratha steams from it. You remove a core element of what makes Uratha known as Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Why don't werewolves don't go around inflicting Lunacy en masse? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MASS LUNACY</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a werewolf induces Lunacy in a crowd, the effect runs the risk of backfiring. A crowd stricken with fear might become an angry mob or a panicked stampede. The Storyteller should make a Resolve + Composure roll for the human with the highest Willpower in the crowd. Success indicates that the person may direct the crowd to some degree. If he simply wants to save himself, the entire crowd follows his lead, but if he is driven violent with fear, the mob might turn against the werewolf. Members of the crowd probably still have problems understanding or remembering exactly what\u2019s happening, but they could be incited to riot or swarm a subject.<br /> This phenomenon is one of the reasons werewolves are unwilling to reveal their presence to humanity. They\u2019ve seen the danger of mob rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Lunacy guarantees that the savage activities of the Forsaken will pass unnoticed by only relying on it? Not at all. The scene of a carnage with bloody footprints which do not match any known animal (Gauru) turning into wolf-paws or a shoe-sole? The witness which actually manages to remember the scene? Investigators <i>will </i>prod at the mystery, and another butchery won't fix things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T13:19:08-08:00","id":64261,"title":"","content":"Putting Gauru on a timer is probably the cludgiest possible way to discourage it's use. It meshes poorly with the the abstract flow of combat and has a gamey-ness that really detracts from the experience. The objective was, as far as I can tell, to make Gauru seem like a short fuse, a risky form that could snap at any second. But a time limit does not accomplish that, instead it makes Gauru a gamable, measurable state that encourages turn counting and meta-gaming.<br /> <br /> It'd be far more effective to add compounding penalties and heightened risk of Death Rage, making it so that every action there is a growing chance the Werewolf will lose control. That, in my mind, makes the form scarier and shifts the focus on to whether it <b>should </b>be used, not how long it can be used for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T15:46:21-08:00","id":64362,"title":"","content":"A time limit for the war form I would like but not something massive as they did in WtA. Maybe a scene duration. Hard to imagine one of the Forsaken fighting a Beshilu and then after 60 seconds he reverts and has a giant rat man eating his entrails. Also a bonus if the change happens on the first night of their auspice.<br /> <br /> Lunacy needs to stay. Invoking mankinds reminder of a time long past and that they aren't top dogs is pretty thematic to the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T22:29:48-08:00","id":64611,"title":"","content":"I believe the shifters in War Against the Pure, if they enter war form, can remain in it for X turns, and after that have to roll to avoid falling into death rage if they want to maintain it. I don't have much of an opinion on time limit versus not, save I think Gauru form should be a wild card. Powerful enough to risk assuming but dangerous enough that you should consider when and where you unleash it's fury.<br /> <br /> I tend to be a fan of lunacy; it's by no means a fool proof system and werewolves still have to be careful. While the Masquerade is more social convention, vampires look human and have access to most of their powers without obviously displaying supernatural elements. A werewolf has no such luck, requiring him to change his shape, and the lunacy helps explain why humans aren't widely aware of the uratha in this modern age of recording devices and technology. I'm looking forward to the Idigam Chronicle where I'm sure they'll come up with their own variant, especially curious to see how the werewolves predatory aura works in the new book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-03T23:15:27-08:00","id":64627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowlost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=64362#post64362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A time limit for the war form I would like but not something massive as they did in WtA. Maybe a scene duration. Hard to imagine one of the Forsaken fighting a Beshilu and then after 60 seconds he reverts and has a giant rat man eating his entrails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that 60 seconds is 20 rounds of combat. I've never seen a 1-on-1 fight in the nWOD last 20 rounds. And it isn't like the time running out on Gauru meant you had to revert to Hishu, you could shift to any form you wanted. Downgrading to Urshul should still leave you in plenty of good shape to keep fighting.<br /> <br /> A 1-on-1 between a decently combat capable Uratha and a Beshilu lasting more than 4-6 rounds would surprise the hell out of me. That's one of the reasons why the time-limit has never really come off as much of an issue as a lot of people seem to make it out to be. nWOD combat (pre- or post-GMC) is pretty short.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T01:06:33-08:00","id":64658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=64627#post64627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind that 60 seconds is 20 rounds of combat. I've never seen a 1-on-1 fight in the nWOD last 20 rounds. And it isn't like the time running out on Gauru meant you had to revert to Hishu, you could shift to any form you wanted. Downgrading to Urshul should still leave you in plenty of good shape to keep fighting.<br /> <br /> A 1-on-1 between a decently combat capable Uratha and a Beshilu lasting more than 4-6 rounds would surprise the hell out of me. That's one of the reasons why the time-limit has never really come off as much of an issue as a lot of people seem to make it out to be. nWOD combat (pre- or post-GMC) is pretty short.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Time Limit</b><br /> <br /> Oh yeah, I get that most times that most combats don't go on for that long - but for me it's not about the mechanical aspect as much as the thematic one - and when I say that, it's not necessarily the thematic one according to just Forsaken. Werewolves that are portrayed as &quot;Garou&quot; in nature in film/tv/literature only tend to come out of their state by choice, by sun up, by calming down or by death. And not because they're a bit knackered. - Which is how it's always come across to me.<br /> <br /> I honestly would run my games without it, <b>but</b> that being said as there seems to be quite a case both for and against removing the time limit.<br /> <br /> What I think the Chronicle book would really suit as a half way point -and what would be thematic to this book and what has gone before it- is your suggestion of rolling for death rage to keep in it and in control of it. I think losing yourself to it would keep the themes in tact. It also allows is both a time limit <i>and </i>an unlimited duration, depending on your point of view.<br /> <br /> Now how long it would take before you start rolling for it, and how much of a penalty you would take is another and different debate I think, especially if the Chronicle is anything like B&amp;S and GMC where a lot of combat and rolls in general can come down to a chance die without the expenditure of hard to return Willpower points. - If I have any of that wrong I'm sorry, been awhile since I've had the core in hands.<br /> <br /> So basically I think that folk who like a limited time, and those who don't, might be able to find some middle ground here. There is of course then always the point where folk who liked the older rules of a time limit can stick with that, and those who don't can just take out a time limit and have elder garou sitting around smoking their peace pipes never quite sure when the other might try to rip them a new one.<br /> <br /> <b>Lunacy</b><br /> <br /> With Lunacy I think it's harder. There seem to be folk who<i> really don't like it </i>and want it gone, and others who <i>really do like it and want it to stay.</i> There's no real middle ground, except if you change it thematically and have it as an active power, which again some people <i>really like</i> (and think it's reminiscent of the new Predatory Aura rules for B&amp;S in a way) and some who<i> really don't</i>.<br /> <br /> My preference for getting rid of it, or at least really toning it down is that<br /> <br /> a) werewolves have a lot of natural weaponry and gifts to deal with breaches of their world from humans already.<br /> <br /> b) I think that many of the games in general separate the supernatural from the mortal world too much as it is (Lunacy in Werewolf, Mage's Paradox, Disbelief and Unravelling, Vampires Mas...no I like that one) and that true horror for both mortals and supernatural survival is when you have to go that extra mile to hide yourself knowing there are mortals in the know (or you're a mortal and you have SEEN a werewolf<br /> <br /> c) although the supernatural books are About the supernaturals (obviously), they are surrounded by mortals and have to interact with them on some level nearly all of the time, yet the games almost seem to forget the mortal presence at times. - Of course, this is ultimately down to how the ST of any given game presents this, but I think there should be more of a push to drive home that running around in a werewolf form is going to attract attention, steps have to be taken. It's too easy for a lazy ST to &quot;Lunacy it up&quot; so to speak. - this might also be down to the fact that although you should adjust the numbers up and down for your personal game it always comes across to me that there's a pack in every city block else the spirit world is horribly unmanageable (and by extension if you're playing cross-over, vampires, mages, changelings etc all over the place.<br /> <br /> <b>Thanks</b><b> to everyone</b><br /> <br /> I am really very interested in what folk have to say about this topic. I know Devs are very interested in what fans have to say and that there's a good chance that they'll steer towards what the majority of the fans want (as long as it fits within their vision), and I would rather it be this way even if they go with a change that I really don't like. I know that these topics can get very heated because folk are very passionate about their games, so thanks for keeping it civil so far on on topic. After Mage, I think werewolf is the game that gets the most contention after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T12:02:33-08:00","id":65040,"title":"","content":"Well with the chroniclers guide, you have the option of removing the time limit completely. it wouldnt be for all Uratha, just those who happen to get to the fetish in time (depending on how the players work it). It is a whole scenario though so it does require some build up with some intense complications. But that said, you get war form with no limitations, the way it supposedly used to be when Uratha ran towns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:09:35-08:00","id":65090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a) werewolves have a lot of natural weaponry and gifts to deal with breaches of their world from humans already. </div> </div> </div>Nothing anywhere close to say, vampiric disciplines such as Dominate, or their in-built thrall-making vitae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> b) I think that many of the games in general separate the supernatural from the mortal world too much as it is (Lunacy in Werewolf, Mage's Paradox, Disbelief and Unravelling, Vampires Mas...no I like that one) and that true horror for both mortals and supernatural survival is when you have to go that extra mile to hide yourself knowing there are mortals in the know (or you're a mortal and you have SEEN a werewolf </div> </div> </div>The game is called <b>Forsaken</b>. As I already posted, any objective investigator finding the scene of a werewolf-caused carnage will be a thorn in any pack's side, incoherent would be witnesses aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:24:07-08:00","id":65096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=65090#post65090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing anywhere close to say, vampiric disciplines such as Dominate, or their in-built thrall-making vitae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The game is called <b>Forsaken</b>. As I already posted, any objective investigator finding the scene of a werewolf-caused carnage will be a thorn in any pack's side, incoherent would be witnesses aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what you're getting at with the vampire reference. You're right they do, that's not in dispute - both vampires and werewolves have their own &quot;natural weaponry&quot; I guess. Vampires defense against humans seeing them, the Masquerade, is one of their own making and there's nothing actively supernatural about it unless they're using disciplines to actively prevent people knowing - which they would have to do every time it was breached (or other kind of active clean ups).<br /> <br /> I was discussing at the time whether there was a need for Lunacy to be an active power that you put on people (like I guess Dominate) rather than a passive one.<br /> <br /> The second point I don't understand either. Yes an investigator finding a werewolf-caused carnage scene would indeed be a thorn in a pack side. So would one that actually sees werewolves and remembers them, possibly because they don't have a passive power in Lunacy if it was made an active power that you had to consciously use. I really don't understand &quot;incoherent would be witnesses aside&quot;. Could you explain what you mean here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:46:01-08:00","id":65105,"title":"","content":"He means that even if there are incoherent witnesses floating around, a smart detective can figure out whats going on to an extent. He'd still be able to track evidence (bloody tracks) last person seen with the victim (the uratha in question). Theres a chapter opening in tribes of the moon where a bunch of cops show up with silver to tell a pack of blood talons to shove off another packs territory. Lunacy isn't completely infallible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T13:51:46-08:00","id":65113,"title":"","content":"Ah yes, sorry my bad.<br /> <br /> Yes, I would say they would be able to - I've not read Tribes of the Moon (that and Signs are the two I haven't, but it's been awhile since I went through the rest anyway).<br /> <br /> Lunacy isn't completely infallible - it is pretty potent though. I tend to see it more as &quot;it works on everyone except when the ST needs it to not work for story and dramatic purposes&quot;. I get the whole backfiring in a crowd as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-04T19:42:27-08:00","id":65322,"title":"","content":"Lemme re-phrace that for you:<br /> <br /> <b>Nothing is</b> completely infallible [...] &quot;it works on everyone except when the ST needs it to not work for story and dramatic purposes&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's a Storytelling game. If the focus of the game isn't on drama, then you're better off playing a dungeon crawl hack and slash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:20:17-08:00","id":65525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MeetsInTaverns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=65096#post65096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you're getting at with the vampire reference. You're right they do, that's not in dispute - both vampires and werewolves have their own &quot;natural weaponry&quot; I guess. Vampires defense against humans seeing them, the Masquerade, is one of their own making and there's nothing actively supernatural about it unless they're using disciplines to actively prevent people knowing - which they would have to do every time it was breached (or other kind of active clean ups).</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Even then, vampires have their ability to avoid being photographed or recorded easily as the Beast innately keeps them protected, so they do possess some measure of supernatural occlusion. If not Lunacy then I think werewolves need something that justifies why the world doesn't know about them. Rare though it'd be, say some guy is pre-change, gets into a bar fight at a biker rally, and now there's seventy plus witnesses who saw someone turn into a hulking war form beast, complete with possible video evidence. Given how unsubtle werewolf forms can be I think there has to be some system in place that conceals the</span>m automatically, I don\u2019t like the idea of a specific power that has to be activated just because one or two uratha who forget to do so could reveal the entire race.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:25:39-08:00","id":65527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nickpire84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=65525#post65525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Even then, vampires have their ability to avoid being photographed or recorded easily as the Beast innately keeps them protected, so they do possess some measure of supernatural occlusion. If not Lunacy then I think werewolves need something that justifies why the world doesn't know about them. Rare though it'd be, say some guy is pre-change, gets into a bar fight at a biker rally, and now there's seventy plus witnesses who saw someone turn into a hulking war form beast, complete with possible video evidence. Given how unsubtle werewolf forms can be I think there has to be some system in place that conceals the</span>m automatically, I don\u2019t like the idea of a specific power that has to be activated just because one or two uratha who forget to do so could reveal the entire race.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point, especially in regard to the changes in B&amp;S.<br /> <br /> I am not trying to argue a point for a certain type of change. I am wanting to hear what other people think and see if a discussion can be had on the topic.<br /> <br /> If the devs kepts Lunacy, what if any changes do people think should be changed, if anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:44:26-08:00","id":65536,"title":"","content":"Nah, I understand what you mean <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. My own personal opinion is just that they need something automatic to maintain a suspension of disbelief (granted we're already pretending such monsters are real...).<br /> <br /> Could leave Lunacy as-is, no change, which was itself a port over from Apocalypse.<br /> Could go with a system like Changing Breed/War Against the Pure offered, where observers roll their Resolve + Composure with werewolf's Primal Urge acting as a penalty (and possibly other modifiers granted by which form was used).<br /> Given the introduction of Conditions, and how they relate to the Kiss for vampires, whatever form Lunacy takes in Idagam Chronicle will likely inflict a Condition, perhaps a combination selective amnesia or hysteria effect.<br /> <br /> I'll admit, I'm hard pressed to think of a middle ground for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1385-nickpire84","name":"Nickpire84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1385_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T03:47:54-08:00","id":65540,"title":"","content":"I'll have to check the War Against the Pure, it's been a long time and I don't even recall a different system. I'd check the Changing Breeds book but I think I might die from dust exposure.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if there are different ways for humans to react towards Lunacy (can't remember if it's all that different in Spirit Slayers for Vigil) then there's obviously the ability to change it. I guess it's whether or not people want it changed, and what they want from the change.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I think it will definitely inflict a condition even if it remains true to the original core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T06:48:48-08:00","id":65635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nickpire84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=65525#post65525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [FONT=Helvetica]Even then, vampires have their ability to avoid being photographed or recorded easily as the Beast innately keeps them protected, so they do possess some measure of supernatural occlusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Nevermind vampires don't even leave fingerprints behind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T02:04:56-08:00","id":67064,"title":"","content":"I think Lunacy as an idea is good, terror at seeing something clearly supernatural AND clearly triggering all deeply buried reflexes to run (because it is a hunter and you are the prey) works.<br /> <br /> I think it should be a bit more generous though, mostly to make things a bit easier for Hunters and the like.<br /> With the system as is, you NEED to be of near perfect willpower to really be a threat to a werewolf (or you can use the optional rules, which bring the threshold down a bit), which I think is a bit too easy.<br /> <br /> Toning it down a bit, maybe adding some modifiers so that it makes it easier for the enemy hunter (and still potent on, say, the crowd of angry bikers) would be nice.<br /> <br /> I do not think it should be an active power, but maybe having gifts to augment it would work well (which then would need to be activated).<br /> <br /> <br /> Remembering the second book of the Dresden Files, I think even with just normal fear and such and the general desire of almost any supernatural group not to have the supernatural made public, it is not that hard to make no one really believing in Werewolves, Vampires and the like work in the current age.<br /> <br /> Though, I think one thing should not be overlooked.<br /> Lunacy, like its predecessor the Delirium, should always be a hindrance as well as a tool.<br /> For every mess up it covers, it also can end up driving humans you wanted to protect right into the arms of danger because they panicked, it is what makes relationships with normal mortals very difficult, it is what potentially drives even your wolfblooded family away...<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Gauru, I am all for scrapping the limit.<br /> I found the near Wolf useful enough the way it was in Apocalypse, with the near Man filling for fancy weapon use (but, admittedly, being the ones form I always thought least useful in both lines).<br /> It is also what people usually expect when they think &quot;werewolf in a fight&quot;.<br /> I do think making it a form were Death Rage is more likely, limiting the use of tools (not to a ridiculous extend) and maybe giving the other forms their niches should suffice.<br /> Let the near wolf make use of its greater dexterity to give them more defence (higher instead of lower of dex/wits), maybe give them the better bite again and do not neglect the fact that they really can move fast (both better Ini as well as better speed).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2094-ray-white","name":"Ray White","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T15:04:45-08:00","id":68092,"title":"","content":"I took the timer off personally; there's no hard limit. You get a grace period of your Stamina + Primal Urge (though this may be shifted to Resolve + Primal Urge as a possibility to reflect less physical strain and more &quot;I'm fighting not to drop into Death Rage everytime I go this route&quot;), and every turn past that (without Instinct or Gift etc. usage) increases Death Rage penalties by -1 for provocations cumulatively in the scene. So long as you can &quot;Keep your partial cool&quot; you're good to go, but in actual gameplay it means that you still don't want to constantly run around in that form; you're gonna snap, and it's gonna be -really- ugly, so most use it sparingly regardless of any exhaustion or hard &quot;unless you Death Rage, you're done&quot;.<br /> <br /> I've always seen as adopting the Gauru form as pretty much Riding the Wave ala Vampire anyhow; I'm not too big on a hard once per scene or x number of turns limitation for it, I much prefer something more Risk vs Reward to tempt players to skirt the line. The more you use it scene, the more aggressive you become until you snap. I'm with PenDragon on this one; in the meantime this seems to be the best solution for me to deal with an inbetween &quot;Can't just run around in it without issues, but have extended times and more chances to adopt it&quot;. Want to keep using it for prolonged periods? Prepare to hunt and kill uncontrollably unless you've really got a good grip on yourself.<br /> <br /> As for Lunacy; I just wrapped what it was into the Predatory Aura; it has Fight, Flight and Competitive as aspects; I could see a bonus to its use being added on while in Gauru though if one wanted to reinforce that it's that much more raw rage, terror and so on, even if just to the Flight lash-out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 02-08-2014, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T13:24:44-08:00","id":69340,"title":"","content":"I like time being limited, it makes Gauru much more thematically interesting. You take the form of power, but you do so at the cost of extreme risk at loosing control and try to murder all around you. Keep in mind that there is no time limit in how long you can keep the form, you can run around in it all night in horrible slaying rage if you want. Now the form may need to be made more powerful to make it truly terrifying (both to ones enemies and to ones friends.)<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to Lunacy I would make it more risky, I would have a chance for the victims of it to go into uncontrolled rage mode and try to murder you rather then into covering in fear mode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/724-palp","name":"Palp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar724_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T16:29:12-08:00","id":70122,"title":"","content":"A house rule I've recently trying out is removing the effect Stamina+Primal Urge limit on Gauru. Instead, you simply roll a cumulative number of dice for every turn you're in. So 1 turn/1 dice, 2 turns-2 dice, and so on. If you hit your Harmony rating in successes (or your Resolve+Primal urge, whichever is higher) then you immediately fall to Death Rage. No take-backsies, no quick shift to another form. Just a Death Rage.<br /> <br /> What I've found is it gives a risk-vs-reward scenario. You no longer know exactly how long you're going to be in Gauru, and you could push your luck if you've got a High Harmony rating; but every roll of the dice is a potential doomsday button. Gifts that add extra turns in Gauru or remove turns just affect the dice. If you remove 3 turns from someone's roll, then they start out immediately with 3 dice on their plate and go from there. If your auspice moon gives you extra turns, you don't roll the dice until you've hit that buffer.<br /> <br /> So far, it's been fairly interesting! But I'm always eyeballing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T20:29:45-08:00","id":70252,"title":"","content":"I've used the hack in Armory Reloaded before it was printed for adding the risk/reward scenario. I've found it fairly effective, especially since it at least allows a few turns before you start rolling for the gamble. Having to roll an extra roll every turn until you shift out or Death Rage is a bit annoying; especially if the odds are incredibly small for the first few rolls anyway. It also allows the moon phase to continue to matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T00:56:34-08:00","id":71093,"title":"","content":"Reading through the flavor text in the core book it seems to me that the war-form was intended to be a form that you didn't want to use if you didn't have to thematically. I feel like they were almost tempted to just not allow it as a form that you could slip into voluntarily, that it was what you became when you lost all control, but obviously that would run too much against the grain. Even I would have grimaced had that been rendered the case and I kind of like the idea, as strange as that sounds. <br /> <br /> I could perhaps stomach a mechanic similar to Riding the Wave that vampires have, reigning in one's rage however briefly into a kind of lucid fury. Something a newly Changed werewolf might struggle with but also something that as they grow older and more powerful manage to bring under a degree of control. However, to balance things out, when an elder wolf does fall to <i>kuruth</i> it should be cataclysmic. If the mechanics were elegant and fun, this I would not mind. I might even love it.<br /> <br /> As it is currently, barring updates from the GMC, the main problem with the war-form is not the time limit. It's clunky and intrusive and game-y, but it functions. The main problem is the lack of extra attacks whilst in it; if you want to optimize damage, pick a fighting style that allows you to make extra attacks. With the proper merits, both Dalu and Urshul forms become more deadly than Gauru even with the stat differences. The main benefit of the war-form is that it's somewhat tankier, not that it can dish out more damage. This is a thematic breakdown for the game.<br /> <br /> Now so far in the GMC-books that have come out, extra-attacks seem to be done away with. None of the fighting styles currently written using it (the GMC rules) allow for them and I've yet to see any powers or rules that allow for it (if I'm wrong somebody please tell me, I've been known to miss pretty important things on first read-throughs of books). As such a direct translation would at least return Gauru to a sort of theoretically optimal combat form, but that would be a pretty immense cop-out considering the opportunity presented. Beefing it up, perhaps making it scale better in various ways, and ultimately making it more risky whilst doing away with the time limit are all things I'm in favor for.<br /> <br /> Completely unnecessary to the conversation, but the way it's handled in the larp is thus: There's a damage cap, both a soft one that's pertinent to your character and a hard one that's universal. The hard damage cap is 5, so even with a beastly built character you can only ever do 5 damage in a single turn. To beef up Gauru form, they doubled the equipment modifiers of its natural attacks (so +4 bite and +2 claw) plus a +2 to your damage cap, thus raising the hard cap to 7. It's very gamey and meta, but it does make Gauru form genuinely terrifying and regardless of your character's build objective the most potentially dangerous. I wouldn't recommend this sort of system for a table-top, but I thought it worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> As for Lunacy, I'd like to see it altered somewhat but not done away with. Supernaturals do need ways to keep themselves secret from mortal society, whether they're built into their templates or arise from internal factions that make certain that it just never hits youtube. I've never been a fan with how Lunacy works as is, the fact that mortals can just sort of graduate out of it essentially means there's an upper echelon of hunters that you actually need to worry about and then a whole slew that will crap their pants immediately if you go Gauru. Giving it modifiers, conditions, and allowing the werewolf to manipulate it in some way would be interesting but ultimately I'd like to see it be something that the character doesn't <i>actually</i> have any control over.<br /> <br /> My recommendation? Tie it to the effect that Primal Urge has on normal mortals. Newly Changed werewolves give off a slight but tangible predatory aura that unnerves people even when in human form, but nothing that would incite a bout of temporary insanity that witnessing Gauru should. Meanwhile elders can barely go into town even in their human form without causing bouts of bedlam in the local population. As previously mentioned, adding powers and merits that allowed a werewolf to further manipulate it would be pretty boss too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:36:47-08:00","id":71276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Red 9</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/63827-removing-luncay-and-gauru-time-limit?p=71093#post71093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now so far in the GMC-books that have come out, extra-attacks seem to be done away with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. There's no hard rule here, but the current authors have been pretty adamant about keeping extra-attacks out of the system outside of automatic fire capable weapons.<br /> <br /> While I have a feeling that FS: Merits are most likely going to keep to avoiding extra-attacks, I wouldn't be surprised to see them enter into the game as parts of supernatural powers. Though, a high level Gift that grants some extra-attacks could easily be written to be useable in Gauru form; so that wouldn't present the same problem multiple attack Merits in the pre-GMC rules caused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As such a direct translation would at least return Gauru to a sort of theoretically optimal combat form, but that would be a pretty immense cop-out considering the opportunity presented. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd say it is a cop-out. I think it is a missed opportunity since it was pretty clear that Gauru wasn't quite badass enough in its original form, but as I've noted previously the changes in GMC era combat generally boost Gauru form considerably more than the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-13T07:47:38-08:00","id":71287,"title":"","content":"I don't think extra attack is the way forward - just from a mechanical standpoint really, I've just never been a fan and don't want to see the return of multiple actions. If they were to boost Garou form thematically that way then I would suggest something similar to the way celerity works in B&amp;S.<br /> <br /> However, that's now really leading to a discussion on extra attacks rather than time limit and lunacy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}